# variants/base/portage/package.use/21-virt — virtualization.
#
# Numeric prefix: Portage reads this directory in sorted order and the LAST
# file wins a conflict (measured 2026-09-13), so the number is precedence, not
# decoration. Ranges: 00-09 hardware · 10-19 languages and toolchain ·
# 20-39 system and graphics · 40-49 applications · 50-69 axis and flavor
# layers · 90-99 late overrides.
#
# These five flags used to be a VIRTUALIZATION group in the global USE. Measured
# against the 1763-package kde plan, each is declared by one or two packages --
# they were never statements about the distribution, only qemu/libvirt
# configuration written where it reached everything. A global flag also catches
# any FUTURE package declaring the same name, silently.
app-emulation/qemu spice usbredir virtfs
app-emulation/libvirt qemu virt-network
sys-firmware/ipxe qemu
net-misc/remmina spice
net-misc/spice-gtk usbredir
